e media  broadcasts  it's completely impossible for anyone in  north korea to just sort of  start a channel and upload these videos  without there being official approval  for it  in the last couple of years other  accounts have emerged on the internet  and una's videos are not staged like the  broadcast created by north korean state  media  she doesn't sit behind an anchor desk  and is often outside  some of the videos even include blooper  moments  [Applause]  north korea seems to be slowly evolving  in the way that it's trying to tell its  story to the world  we're 20 years into the 21st century but  i think this is the first 21st century  style propaganda that north korea has  tried  for the international audience though it  couldn't be determined who's exactly  behind these channels  echo of truth and new dprk are now  drawing more than 37 000 followers  on chinese social media platform weibo  the new dprk account has more than half  a million followers  analysts say this evolution of north  korean propaganda  is probably inspired by china  in the next 20 days we'll take a grand  road trip which also tightly controls  its media to sway opinion at home and  abroad we'll also learn tonka scroll  painting horseback riding  knife making and dancing they are taking  a page from china's propaganda book  it's a little bit easier for them to to  look at chinese social networks and see  what's popular  and kind of take that as ideas among the  several dozen videos uploaded this year  one theme has come up frequently the  fake news is the last  thing we need in such fierce battle time  with call it 19.  these videos debunk what outsiders have  said about north korea's handling  of the coronavirus outbreak a world food  program report from april  placed north korea on a list of  countries at risk of food shortages  because of the pandemic  a few days later una took viewers to a  supermarket in pyongyang  as you can see all the shops are fully  stocked with products and food to  satisfy people's demand  north korea's economy was already hit by  sanctions and economists say the  pandemic will likely hurt growth this  year  recently a western media reported  about dprk's economy so i'm here today  to  check it out luna asked shoppers if  everyday items are getting too expensive  traditionally north korea hasn't  directly responded to much  press coverage and much international  criticism what we've seen on these  youtube channels is they're trying to  put a little bit of doubt into your mind  but you know maybe everything you see on  north korea isn't quite true  north korean authorities have also  repeatedly claimed the country has had  zero coronavirus infections  though state media reported one apparent  case that was imported by a defector who  had returned in july  four media and north korea watchers have  been skeptical about the claim  there's a lot of suspicion that kovid  has already been  present in north korea for many months  now the entire world is now watching  with amazement and disbelief  in this video from march una explained  the regime's secrets to stopping the  virus  the message from north korea was that  this sort of  well-running society they having this  this efficient government i have  our respective supreme leader has  foreign at the very beginning  an efficient health system that's able  to maintain  hygiene levels which other countries  weren't able to do  it's hard to tell how effectively north  korea's new propaganda will sway  foreigners  but una's youtube channel is already  getting many more views than another one  of the regime's state media accounts  that was set up around the same time  in 2017. i think if the audience  continues growing  i think the next thing you'll see is  north korea putting a bit more money  into some of these videos  and they're going to continue trying to  refine it because the same as any  propaganda it's all about international  public image  the nation the land the freedom